      "ImageDescription": {
        "value": "This brown algae <em>Dictyota dichotoma</em> , which can reach 10 to 25 cm in length (max. 50 cm), grows like all algae, by absorbing the mineral salts contained in the water through the process of photosynthesis.</p><p> The thallus is flattened into strips and the branching is dichotome: the branches are of the same length. Its color varies from brown to green and is characterized by a blue iridescence during its vegetative growth phase, visible only underwater.</p><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p> The colony was photographed in the artificial reefs of the port of La Seyne-sur-Mer.",
